<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>

<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Constitution of the Order</title>

<style>

body{
    background:white;
    color:#111;
    font-family: "Times New Roman", serif;
    line-height:1.7;
    margin:0;
}

.page{
    max-width:850px;
    margin:auto;
    padding:80px 60px;
}

.title{
    text-align:center;
    font-size:34px;
    letter-spacing:2px;
}

.subtitle{
    text-align:center;
    font-size:18px;
    margin-top:10px;
}

.rule{
    border:none;
    border-top:1px solid #000;
    margin:35px auto;
    width:70%;
}

.divider{
    text-align:center;
    margin:30px 0;
    font-size:16px;
}

h3{
    margin-top:40px;
}

.rank-list{
    margin:25px 0;
}

.rank-list li{
    margin:6px 0;
}

.signature{
    margin-top:70px;
}

.signature-name{
    margin-top:20px;
}

.stamps{
    display:flex;
    justify-content:space-between;
    align-items:flex-end;
    margin-top:80px;
}


.stamps img{
    width:120px;
    opacity:0.9;
}

.center-seal{
    text-align:center;
}

.motto{
    text-align:center;
    font-style:italic;
    margin-top:40px;
}



.signature{
    margin-top:70px;
}

.signature-area{
    position:relative;
    width:320px;
    margin-top:25px;
}

.signature-line{
    border-bottom:2px solid black;
    width:320px;
}


.signature-img{
    position:absolute;

    left:140px;   
    top:-105px;   

    width:130px; 

    transform:rotate(-2deg);
    opacity:0.95;
    filter: grayscale(0);
}



.centered{
    text-align:center;
}




#stamps{
    position:relative;
    height:140px; 
    margin-top:10px; 
}

/* main stamp */
.stamp-large{
    position:absolute;
    left:0;
    bottom:0;
    padding-left: 350px;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
    width:350px;
    transform:rotate(-4deg);
    opacity:1;
}

/* seal overlapping signature */
.seal-small{
    position:absolute;
    right:0;
    bottom:-20px;
    width:120px;
    transform:rotate(3deg);
    opacity:0.9;
}

#logo{
    width: 200px;
}

.logo {text-align: center;}

</style>

</head>



<body>

<div class="page">

    <div class="logo">
<img id="logo" src="/images/bwlogo.jpg" alt="">
</div>

<h1 class="title">
CONSTITUTION OF <br> ORDO PRAECONUM CAMPANAE LEONIS
</h1>

<p class="subtitle">
</p>

<hr class="rule">

<div class="divider">✶ ✶</div>


<h3>I — Purpose of the Order</h3>

<p>
1. To investigate mysteries of philosophy, science, history, and consciousness.<br>
2. To preserve and transmit knowledge between generations.<br>
3. To serve as a collective of individuals dedicated to wisdom and discovery.
</p>

<p>
The Organisation does not concern itself with temporary politics or worldly disputes.
</p>


<div class="divider">✶ ✶</div>


<h3>II — Core Virtues</h3>

<p>
<strong>Humility</strong><br>
<strong>Perseverance</strong><br>
<strong>Sharing</strong><br>
<strong>Gratitude</strong>
</p>

<p>
Heralds of the Lion's Bell swear to remain humble sages.  
These four virtues form the pillars of the Herald.
</p>

<p>
For this reason, being a Herald must never be treated as an honor, although
it is one of the highest degree.
</p>


<div class="divider">✶ ✶</div>


<h3>III — Structure of the Order</h3>

<p><strong>Outer Circle</strong></p>

<ul class="rank-list">
<li>Seekers</li>
<li>Akousmatikoi</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Inner Circle</strong></p>

<ul class="rank-list">
<li>Heralds</li>
<li>Keepers of the Bell</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Inner Sanctum</strong></p>

<ul class="rank-list">
<li>Supreme Herald</li>
<li>The Lion</li>
</ul>


<br>

<p><strong>Seekers</strong></p>
<p>
Individuals who show interest in the order and are starting on the lions journey,
but not yet fully pledged members of the Order.
</p>

<p><strong>Akousmatikoi</strong></p>
<p>
Those that have began their journey and started to listen,
just like the great Pythagoras once taught them.
</p>

<p><strong>Heralds</strong></p>
<p>
Full members of the order. They have given their life to study and now they live in duty of sharing and contributing humanity.
</p>
</p>

<p><strong>Keepers of the Bell</strong></p>
<p>
Senior members entrusted with safeguarding the traditions and teachings of the Order and protecting the integrity of knowledge and the institution.
</p>
</p>

<br>

<p>
The Order is guided by its founder and leader.
There can not be another Lion, as he is the reincarnation of the great Sage. <br> <br>


In the founder’s absence the Supreme Herald and the Keepers of the Bell serve as
the guiding authority of the Order. <br>

<br>

In the years 11700 since the Collapse,
<strong> The Lion of the Order is Lekistra.</strong>
</p>


<div class="divider">✶ ✶</div>


<p class="motto">
Campana Sonat Omnibus
</p>

<div class="signature">

<p>Signed and affirmed,</p>

<div class="signature-area">

<div class="signature-line"></div>

<img class="signature-img" src="/images/signature.png" alt="Signature">

</div>

<p class="signature-name">
<strong>Lekistra</strong><br>
The Founder
</p>

</div>



<div id="stamps">

<img class="stamp-large" src="/images/bwstamp.jpg" alt="OLB stamp">

<img class="seal-small" src="/images/seal ink.png" alt="OPCL seal">

</div>



</body>
</html>
